    "solution": "Use the low wavedash and pod crossing learned in F55 to reach the eastern pier. Climb the vertical hinge and cut down at its hub as you crest it; the climb turns into a six-tile launch runway. Step left for room, dash down-right along it, then jump left after the ground contact restores your dash. This reverse hyper stays beneath the upper thorn roof and above the descending patrol. Carry its momentum, dash left to the returning moth, and cut with Jump held. Loft and spend the new dash up-left through the final patrol lane to the home balcony.",
    "nearestExisting": "F55 teaches the exact lower launch phrase, while B55 introduces meeting a returning moth. F56 combines those learned arrivals with a reverse launch from architecture the knight changed on the outbound climb. F49 has a folded return but uses a collapsing seam; F56 instead makes the same hinged body a climb and then a launch runway.",
    "novelty": "The first phrase prepares both the player and the room: the visible climb becomes the floor needed to build the upper return. The reverse launch must preserve a dash for a second airborne extension before the moving target supplies the final loft and resource reset.",
