    "designNotes": "The lower roof has visible thorns on both faces so its top cannot become an ordinary bypass. The upper roof limits ordinary jump height. An active short-hop/dash from the nearest converted-runway edge falls short; an ordinary jump/dash from the unturned hinge also fails. The small air pocket east of the hinge removes the immediate wall against which its narrow vertical head could otherwise replenish a dash. Advanced alternate routes have not been exhaustively searched; no event receipt is used to seal the exit.",
    "endingForgiveness": "The return is the more demanding half: reverse launch, retained-dash extension, moving interception and final rising dash. Its last departure succeeds four frames earlier and later, and four extra observation frames on the converted runway also succeed. The challenge remains in the sequence rather than a single contact frame.",
